PROVENANCE

The files in this directory and below it are yhc's own regression tests: the programs of
tests/conformance98 in the repository of yhc, the York Haskell Compiler, which grew from nhc98.
Three of them (Enum/succ, IO/overwrite, layout/tullsen3) share their names with tests of nhc98's
tests/conformance98, but their files differ.

They are vendored here without a licence, under the rule of this repository's owner, quoted:

    "If you want to vendor code without a license add a PROVENANCE alongside it instead."

rhc, the Haskell 98 compiler of this repository, compiles and runs them in its tests
(tests/hs/corpus: the programs of D56 of the haskell98 roadmap, which tests/hs/corpus/licences.tsv
lists with this file as their notice).

Upstream
    repository  https://github.com/haskell-implementations/yhc.git
    commit      c669451c1cb60193f61fe897a301de633f674be3, as tests/hs/corpus/trees.tsv pins it
    path        tests/conformance98/ in that repository: a file at P below this directory
                is tests/conformance98/P upstream
    fetched     2026-10-27, by git clone; the pinned commit was the head it fetched
    copied      2026-11-10, byte for byte, by `bin/rune-test hs-corpus-vendor`; the nightly test
                hs-corpus/vendored compares every file here with the pinned tree

Licence
    No licence is stated for these files, and no file of them carries a notice. yhc's repository has
    licence files only for parts of its source (src/libraries/core/LICENSE, and the third-party
    files of src/translator/js), none for its tests; src/compiler98/yhc.cabal says "License: GPL" of
    the compiler.

Programs
    Each program by its id in tests/hs/corpus/candidates.tsv: its files, as paths below this
    directory; then what the files' own headers name of its authors and origin, and any notice,
    quoted as FILE:LINE and the line (tabs expanded, trailing blanks dropped). A program with no
    "named" names no author or origin in its files; one with no "notice" carries none.

